### Roundoff Exercise II




Predict when adding a repeatedly halved positive amount stops changing `x`. Trace the loop and explain its stopping condition. This program uses no method definition.


double x = 1.0;
double amount = 1.0;
int halvings = 0;
while (x + amount != x)
{
    amount /= 2;
    halvings++;
}
Console.WriteLine($"Halvings: {halvings}");
Console.WriteLine($"Addition unchanged: {x + amount == x}");


The example holds `x` fixed while reducing `amount`. The condition tests the stored floating-point result, not exact real-number arithmetic.


